{
  "dom_id": "step-q237266",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Expand the following product.\n\n$(x-2\\sqrt{3})(x+2\\sqrt{3})=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We will use the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)(a-b)={a}^{2}-{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=x$ and $b=2\\sqrt{3},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2\\sqrt{3})(x+2\\sqrt{3}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-(2\\sqrt{3})^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-4\\cdot 3 & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-12. & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
